# .cursorrules — PulseIQ (mirror of CLAUDE.md; keep both in sync)

You are working on PulseIQ, a local-first cardiac screening workspace:
FastAPI (backend/, port 8000) + React 18/Vite/TS (frontend/, port 5173).
No database, no auth, no API keys required. 17 rule-grounded agents.

## Hard rules

- Never require an API key, account, or network. Every LLM path keeps a
  `_local_*` rule-based fallback in backend/ai_assistant.py (three tiers:
  local → Ollama → Gemini; any failure degrades to local).
- Never make symptom extraction depend on spaCy: the curated dictionary in
  agents/nlp_symptom_agent.py is the contract; spaCy is optional.
- Route handlers (backend/api_server.py) must go through
  backend/orchestrator.py — never import clinical agents directly from
  routes. Risk banding (>0.75 High / >0.45 Medium) lives only in the
  orchestrator.
- Agents never import sibling agents; only orchestrator / realtime_service /
  api_server import them.
- data/heart.csv target labels are INVERTED upstream (1 = healthy);
  backend/train_model.py flips and asserts them. Do not "correct" that.
- No new server-side persistence. History = browser localStorage (max 20).
- Domain errors return HTTP 200 with {"error": "..."} — see
  docs/API_SPEC.md conventions. Do not introduce HTTP error codes ad hoc.
- Contract or version changes must update docs/ (API_SPEC.md, TECH_STACK.md)
  in the same change; reversals of decisions need a docs/ADR.md entry.

## Layout map

- backend/: api_server.py (routes) · orchestrator.py (pipeline) ·
  ai_assistant.py (LLM tiers) · realtime_service.py (WS fusion)
- agents/: 17 isolated rule-grounded modules, one concern each
- models/: heart_model.pkl + heart_model_meta.json (never hand-edit)
- frontend/src/: pages/ (routes), components/ (app, BodyPainDiagram,
  Heart3DModel, ui/ shadcn kit), @/ path alias
- docs/: ARCHITECTURE · DATA_FLOW · API_SPEC · ADR · TECH_STACK ·
  COMPATIBILITY · CONVENTIONS · SECURITY

## Verify before done

- Backend: .venv/Scripts/python -m pytest backend -q (Windows venv)
- Frontend: cd frontend && npm run typecheck && npm run build
- UI: npm run ui-audit (contrast, overflow, tap targets)

## Style

- Python: stdlib-first, no new heavy deps without an ADR entry.
- React: functional components + hooks; reuse components/ui; Tailwind for
  layout; lucide-react icons.

## Known device quirk

This laptop's Windows Application Control blocks sklearn _liblinear and
spacy levenshtein (.pyd). A venv-local shim
(.venv/Lib/site-packages/sitecustomize.py) stubs the blocked module so the
model loads and the API serves (recreate it if the venv is rebuilt); spacy
degrades to the dictionary matcher. Don't remove sklearn/shap over it; see
docs/COMPATIBILITY.md.
